It seems to me dealers should not be permitted to sell gas and oil and not provide these comforts for us also. Some travelers would drive all night instead of trying to find lodging in an unfamiliar and possibly dangerous town. They'd pack picnics so they didn't have to stop for food. Some people would even carry portable toilets in the trunks of their cars, knowing that there was a good chance they'd be turned away from roadside restrooms. But since 1936, a guy named Victor Hugo Green had been trying to help with some of these
在我看来，经销商不应该被允许销售汽油和机油，却不为我们提供这些便利。一些旅行者会整夜开车，而不是试图在一个陌生且可能危险的城镇寻找住宿。他们会打包野餐，这样就不必停下来吃饭。有些人甚至会在汽车后备箱里携带便携式马桶，因为他们知道很有可能被路边的洗手间拒之门外。但自1936年以来，一个叫维克多·雨果·格林（Victor Hugo Green）的人一直在试图帮助解决其中一些

