The S-S-O makes your car go! And be mortering! SO, also known as Standard Oil, and now known as ExxonMobile, was one of the few oil companies back then that actively pursued black customers. They franchised their stations to African-American operators, and they had a black representative on staff, James Billboard Jackson, who helped place green books in many of those stations, as well as the White Own ones. S.O. may have done this out of a sense of fairness and equality.
S-S-O让你的车跑起来！还有汽车！SO，也就是标准石油公司（Standard Oil），现在被称为埃克森美孚（ExxonMobil），是当时少数几家积极争取黑人客户的石油公司之一。他们将加油站特许经营给非裔美国经营者，并且在员工中有一位黑人代表，詹姆斯·比尔博德·杰克逊（James Billboard Jackson），他帮助将《绿皮书》放置在许多这些加油站，以及白人拥有的加油站中。SO这样做可能是出于一种公平和平等的意识。

