00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:35.000
John DeRocquefeller, who founded Standard Oil in 1870, had married into a family of abolitionists who were part of the underground railroad, and he'd voted for Abraham Lincoln back in the day. But SO probably did it for another reason too. Money honey, it has to do with money. Remember Curtis, who had the crappy experience driving across East Texas? His dad operated one of the first black owned SO associations in New Orleans where Curtis was born and raised. It was called Bootsie and Buddies. The economic logic of stocking the green book was pretty simple, he says.
1870年创立标准石油公司的约翰·洛克菲勒（John D. Rockefeller），娶了一个废奴主义者家庭的女儿，他们是地下铁路的一部分，而且他当年还投票支持过亚伯拉罕·林肯。但SO这样做可能还有另一个原因。钱，亲爱的，这和钱有关。还记得那个在德克萨斯州东部开车经历糟糕的柯蒂斯吗？他的父亲在柯蒂斯出生和长大的新奥尔良经营着第一批黑人拥有的SO加油站之一。它叫“靴子和伙伴”（Bootsie and Buddies）。他说，储备《绿皮书》的经济逻辑很简单。

