00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:36.000
And it gave you a sense of security. And so the green book came to cover listings in all 50 states and even some locations in Canada, the Caribbean and Mexico. They printed about 15,000 copies a year. Victor Green had changed travel for thousands of African-American tourists. He wrote in a 1956 introduction to the guide. Now, things are different. The Negro traveler can depend on the Green Book for all the information he wants.
它给了你一种安全感。于是《绿皮书》涵盖了所有50个州的列表，甚至包括加拿大、加勒比地区和墨西哥的一些地点。他们每年印刷约15,000份。维克多·格林改变了成千上万非裔美国游客的旅行方式。他在1956年指南的序言中写道：现在，情况不同了。黑人旅行者可以依靠《绿皮书》获取他想要的所有信息。

